{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N1"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 126, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual input-to-output path where none existed gives large gains, while replacing an existing conv with skip gives small or mixed changes (exps 13,14,20-22 vs 17-19)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "In pooling-dominated cells an extra parameter-free shortcut further dilutes learnable signal and hurts accuracy (exp 15 vs 13,14)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 4 is absent, removing edge 5 severs node 3 from intermediate nodes, collapsing the cell (exps 64,65)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 1 absent, removing edge 0 cuts the only input route to intermediate nodes (exps 30,31)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the direct input-output edge, removing edge 0 drastically reduces connectivity and can disconnect the cell (exps 31,32)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Restoring a missing edge with a 3x3 conv adds capacity and a path, a larger gain than swapping an existing op (exps 4,11,12 vs 1-3,79,80)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without a direct input-output skip, a residual path via node 1 is much more valuable (exps 82,88,90 vs 81,83)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pooling op with a learnable 3x3 conv yields consistent gains (exps 37,38 vs 39,40)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, 